spock2 (0.1.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Start from menu/desktop: config search prefers the user config, a missing
    SPOCK2_CONFIG no longer aborts, and startup errors show a dialog.
  * Settings dialog: scrollable tabs, screen-aware size, TLS section
    (ssl_verify / ca_bundle) plus connection test.
  * Compact typography and multi-column order cards; status bar elides instead
    of cutting words and names the actual error.
  * Print failures are visible: retry delay honoured, failure log with queue and
    reason, banner in the main window, failure counter in the status bar.

 -- SPOCK2 Contributors <spock2@localhost>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 22:40:00 +0200

spock2 (0.1.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Give each thread its own pycups connection (shared libcups socket crashed).
  * Poll printer health in the status thread; CUPS IPP no longer blocks the UI.
  * Enable faulthandler and log PySide/Qt/platform at startup.

 -- SPOCK2 Contributors <spock2@localhost>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 21:40:00 +0200

spock2 (0.1.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.1.1: Ubuntu 26.04 system Python and apt runtime deps.
  * Install into /usr (DEB_PYTHON_INSTALL_LAYOUT=deb), not /usr/local.

 -- SPOCK2 Contributors <spock2@localhost>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 21:14:00 +0200

spock2 (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Packaging for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (resolute): runtime Python deps from apt.
  * Depends: python3-pyside6.qt{core,gui,widgets}, python3-httpx,
    python3-pydantic, python3-tomli-w, python3-cups (no pip/venv).
  * Ships spock2 binary, example config, udev rules, systemd units, kiosk helpers.

 -- SPOCK2 Contributors <spock2@localhost>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
